Fixes the category "Image" field (Catalog > Categories > Content > Category Image) silently losing the
selected image after save when picked via "Select from Gallery", whenever the store's configured
"Base URL for User Media Files" is a separate, absolute domain (e.g. a CDN such as CloudFront) rather than
the store's own domain.

Root cause: Magento\Catalog\Model\Category\Attribute\Backend\Image::fileResidesOutsideCategoryDir()
decides whether the picked image lives inside catalog/category (bare filename, assumed to already be on
disk there) or elsewhere (full path, e.g. the WYSIWYG media gallery) by checking whether the image URL
contains the local media directory's relative URI (e.g. "media") as a substring. When the media base URL
is an absolute CDN domain, the image URL (e.g. https://cdn.example.com/wysiwyg/content/image.jpg) never
contains that substring, so every gallery-picked image is misclassified as already residing in
catalog/category. Magento then stores just the bare filename as the category's image attribute without
ever copying the file there. If no file with that exact name happens to already exist in catalog/category
(e.g. from an earlier direct "Upload"), the category image is saved as a dangling reference: the DB value
looks correct, but Magento\Catalog\Model\Category\FileInfo::isExist() can't find the file on disk, so both
the admin field and the storefront image render as empty.

Fix: fileResidesOutsideCategoryDir() (and the "outside category dir" branch of beforeSave()) now resolve
the image URL to a path relative to the media directory by first trying to strip the store's actually
configured media base URL (StoreManagerInterface::getStore()->getBaseUrl(UrlInterface::URL_TYPE_MEDIA)),
which correctly handles an absolute CDN domain, before falling back to the original relative-URI
substring check for same-domain URLs. The resolved path is then stored as a canonical "/<media dir>/..."
path (e.g. /media/wysiwyg/content/image.jpg) instead of the raw parse_url() path, so it round-trips
correctly through FileInfo's own "is this inside catalog/category or in the media dir" detection on
subsequent loads.

Gotcha: this does not copy any files. It only fixes the attribute value that gets stored so it points
at the image's real, already-existing location, instead of a bare filename inside catalog/category where
no file was ever placed. Category images saved while the bug was present may already have a dangling
bare-filename value and are not fixed retroactively by this patch.

